ropagated, and suitable growing conditions, are unknown and must be established through evidence.\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":\\\"Potential inputs include viable root material and suitable soil; exact requirements are unknown.\\\",\\\"costs\\\":\\\"Method, learning time, labor, material requirements and growth time are unknown; none should be assumed free or instantaneous.\\\",\\\"effects\\\":\\\"Enable actual planting and tending only after any required learning and with real inputs and elapsed growth time. Successful growth and harvest must be observed, not granted by this request.\\\"}},\\\"repeat\\\":1,\\\"until\\\":null,\\\"guard\\\":null}],\\\"repeat\\\":1,\\\"until\\\":null,\\\"interrupts\\\":[],\\\"notes\\\":[\\\"Use known safe roots rather than assuming nuts or acorns are edible.\\\",\\\"Gathering removes finite stock; neither recovery of the patch nor successful cultivation is established.\\\"],\\\"preferences\\\":[\\\"Maintain a reserve of known safe food.\\\",\\\"Prefer low-risk observations before costly physical experiments.\\\"],\\\"projects\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"renewable-food\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"active\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"Can local meadow roots support a renewable food supply?\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"At tick 0, the meadow-root patch at (10.1,12) visibly holds six units.\\\",\\\"Starting knowledge records root nutrition as 14 and toxicity as zero.\\\"],\\\"uncertainty\\\":\\\"Regrowth, propagation requirements, growing time and sustainable yield are unknown.\\\",\\\"goal\\\":\\\"Establish an evidence-based food renewal method while retaining safe food for immediate needs.\\\",\\\"completedSteps\\\":[],\\\"outputs\\\":[],\\\"missing\\\":\\\"Direct observations of the patch and a feasible propagation method.\\\",\\\"next\\\":\\\"Collect a limited reserve, observe the patch and seek a learnable propagation method.\\\",\\\"pauseReason\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"benefit\\\":\\\"No cultivation benefit has yet been demonstrated.\\\"}]}\"}","logprobs":[]}

